;; The interpreter's end (queue 253; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "As built: 253"): Python/pylifecycle.c's
;; Py_FinalizeEx and finalize_modules (CPython 3.14.10), after the main module ran or the REPL ended. In CPython's
;; order: the non-daemon threads joined, the atexit functions, sys.is_finalizing() true and the other threads stopped
;; (a thread that takes the GIL from then on hangs, PyThread_hang_thread), sys.stdout and sys.stderr flushed (exit
;; status 120 when sys.stdout's flush fails), a collection (gc.collect's, its callbacks, unless gc.disable()), the import
;; machinery's caches cleared, then finalize_modules: builtins._ and sys's special names cleared, the standard streams
;; restored, every module taken out of sys.modules (CPython keeps a weak reference to each), the builtins restored to
;; the interpreter's first copy, a collection, the modules still alive cleared in reverse import order (their names
;; with one underscore first, then the others: _PyModule_ClearDict), sys's and builtins' dictionaries cleared last,
;; a last collection; sys.stdout and sys.stderr flushed again.
;;
;; The collections at shutdown: CPython frees the dictionaries of the modules nothing holds any more as cyclic
;; garbage (their functions' globals and their classes make cycles), their objects' __del__ run with every global in
;; place. pyi's classes are held by the runtime's registries (classInfos, subclasses, the inline caches: queue 241's
;; finding 2), so Go's collector would keep every module that defines a class. The module dictionaries that CPython's
;; interpreter state no longer reaches (exitMark: sys, the builtins, the codecs' registry, what they reach through
;; objects, classes, functions and modules) are given to the cycle collector as dead (cyForced): the probe treats them
;; as garbage and an edge into one as reaching nothing, so what they alone hold is found and finalized in PEP 442's
;; order, while anything Go still holds by another way (a held node, a Go value) stays alive. Their dictionaries are
;; not cleared afterwards (CPython's tp_clear): what they hold through no node (a class's attribute, a Go container)
;; stays as it is, silent rather than finalized with its globals gone.


